*  217 - direct goto :<VAR> — transfer to the FIRST statement of a code
*  block built by CODE(), labelled or not (SPITBOL manual v3.7 p.178,
*  "The direct Goto"; p.133 shows the same form). The manual's own idiom
*  is used here: the fragment carries a Goto back into the main program,
*  because execution falling out of the bottom of a code block terminates.
*  Both spellings are exercised — bare :<C> and the spaced :< C >.
        C = CODE("  OUTPUT = 'first block' :(TWO)")
        OUTPUT = 'main'                          :<C>
BAD     OUTPUT = 'NOT REACHED'                   :(END)
TWO     D = CODE("  OUTPUT = 'second block' :(THREE)")
        :< D >
THREE   E = CODE("LBL OUTPUT = 'third block, labelled' :(DONE)")
        :<E>
DONE    OUTPUT = 'back in main'
END
